# Code owners (Q28 staged approval). Later matches win, so the specific paths come last.
#
# >>> SECOND REVIEWER PLACEHOLDER <<<
# Code-owner review is prepared, not enabled. GitHub never lets an author approve their own PR,
# so requiring code-owner review with a single owner would block every merge. When a second
# reviewer (user or team, with write access) exists, add them to every line below, merge that,
# then turn on code-owner review in the main and stable rulesets (see docs/repo-setup.md,
# "Turn on code-owner review").

* @adam-m-holloway

# Stage moves (npm run stage) — the approval that promotes or retires a plugin.
/plugins/*/status.json @adam-m-holloway

# The rules every PR is judged by.
/.github/ @adam-m-holloway
/taxonomy.json @adam-m-holloway
/schema/ @adam-m-holloway
/rules/ @adam-m-holloway
/scripts/ @adam-m-holloway
